  "profileText": "a Representative from Utah; born in Cedar City, Iron County, Utah, May 22, 1981; graduated from Pahranagat Valley High School, Alamo, Nev.; B.S., Southern Utah University, Cedar City, Utah, 2003; J.D., Brigham Young University, J. Reuben Clark Law School, Provo, Utah, 2015; soil conservationist, United States Department of Agriculture, 2001-2012; deputy attorney, Washington County, Utah, 2015-2018; attorney, Utah Association of Counties, 2016-2018; attorney, Washington County Water Conservancy District, Utah, 2018-2019; staff, United States Representative Chris Stewart of Utah, 2019-2023; elected as a Republican to the One Hundred Eighteenth Congress, by special election, to fill the vacancy caused by the resignation of United States Representative Chris Stewart, and reelected to the succeeding Congress (November 21, 2023-present).",
